IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g4-art11-application`
IMPORT `g4-art11-decision`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-art19-reportable-matters`
IMPORT `g6-art20-court-orders`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `int-readings`
IMPORT `int-nouns`
IMPORT `int-commencement`
IMPORT `int-vintage`
IMPORT `int-wiring`

-- int-h-application.l4: headline (a) of the integration layer: may this application for registration be granted?
-- Article 11(4) lists the matters on which the Commissioner must register an applicant that complies with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5): the charity test (group G2, Article 5), the Jersey
-- entity or substantial Jersey activity (Article 11(4)(c)), the principal address in Jersey (Article 11(4)(d); group G3, Article 8(4)), the name (Article 12(1); group G4), and the findings of the Commissioner.
-- Beside them stand two bars on GRANTING that Article 11(4) does not list (trap T10): a reported fitness issue about a governor that is undetermined or whose order or notice is not complied with
-- (Article 19(9)(c); group G6) and a court order that the entity must not be registered (Article 20(1)(c); group G6). Group G4 decides how the duty to register meets the bars (fork F4.4); this module supplies
-- the bars (IP23, IP24) from group G6, and everything else from the group that decides it. The application's completeness is Article 11(2) (G4) and Article 19(5) (G6, IP22).
-- It rests on Articles 2, 5, 6, 7, 8, 11, 12, 19 and 20, and refuses for a day before the last of them was in force (1 May 2018 for the Articles of Parts 4 and 5; 21 November 2014 for the rest).

§ `Integration layer -- headline (a): may this application be granted?`

-- The case: an applicant, its application and the facts and opinions that the Articles read.
DECLARE `Application in the case` HAS
    body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The applicant and its people (standing: an applicant for registration); the kinds of entity, Jersey-entity status and governors are derived
    `charity test facts` IS A `Facts for the charity test in the case` @desc The constitution facts, the public benefit determination and the Article 5(3) Order for the charity test (Article 5)
    application IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
    findings IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` @desc The Commissioner's findings on the matters of Article 11(4) that no other group decides, and on the grounds prescribed under Article 11(7)
    `Order under Article 13(9)` IS A MAYBE `Order under Article 13(9)` @desc The Order under Article 13(9) that applies to registered charities (payment details, statement of intentions, entry on the register); NOTHING if none
    `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS A LIST OF `Order under Article 13(10)` @desc The Orders under Article 13(10) that relieve small charities
    `facts for the principal address` IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` @desc The registered office, the main premises and the governors' addresses in Jersey (Article 8(4))
    `opinion on the name` IS AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` @desc The Commissioner's opinion on the proposed registered name (Article 12(1))
    `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report (Article 19(5))
    `orders of the court` IS A LIST OF `Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` @desc The orders the court has made under Article 20(1)
    `notices served` IS A LIST OF `Notice served in the case` @desc The required steps notices served on the applicant's governors or on a charity in which they were governors (Article 19(1)(a) reads them)

-- The answer: the decision and every ground it rests on, so that a caller can see which ground failed.
DECLARE `Answer on an application for registration` HAS
    entity IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it (IP5): kinds of entity, Jersey-entity status, governors with their reportable matters
    `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP8, group G2: Article 5
    `the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Group G4: Article 11(2) (and the Order of Article 13(9)(b) on the statement of intentions, IP29)
    `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP22, group G6: Article 19(5)
    `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP15, group G4: a Jersey entity, or an activity in or from within Jersey that is substantial
    `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP16, group G4: a principal address in Jersey
    `the entity has a principal address in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP17, group G3: Article 8(4)
    `the name is undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18, group G4: Article 12(1)
    `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP23, group G6
    `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP24, group G6: Article 20(1)(c)
    duty IS A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration` @desc What the Commissioner must or must not do with the application (group G4, Article 11(4) and (5) against the bars)
    decision IS A MAYBE `Decision of the Commissioner` @desc The decision of the Commissioner as other provisions name it (IP27); NOTHING where neither duty arises
    `the application may be granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE exactly when the Commissioner must register the applicant (the duty of Article 11(4) arises and no bar on granting displaces it)

-- The answer under ONE text of the Law (the text decides the kinds of entity: sub-paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1)).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law
      case IS AN `Application in the case` @desc The case
GIVETH AN `Answer on an application for registration`
`Int (a) the answer on the application under the text` readings day vintage case MEANS
    `Answer on an application for registration` WITH
        entity IS entity
        `the entity meets the charity test` IS charityTest
        `the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` IS `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` (readings's `reading of Articles 11 and 12`) (case's application) orderB
        `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` IS complied
        `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` IS `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` entity ((case's findings)'s `applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey`) ((case's findings)'s `activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial`)
        `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` IS `Art 11(4)(d) the requirement is met` address
        `the entity has a principal address in Jersey` IS address
        `the name is undesirable` IS undesirable
        `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` IS bars
        `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` IS ordered
        duty IS duty
        decision IS `Art 11 what the Commissioner must do on the application` (readings's `reading of Articles 11 and 12`) (case's application) orderB complied entity charityTest (case's findings) address undesirable bars ordered
        `the application may be granted` IS duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
    WHERE
        notices MEANS `Int IP19 the required steps notices served` readings (case's `notices served`)
        entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day (case's body)
        charityTest MEANS `Int IP8 the entity meets the charity test` readings vintage entity ((case's body)'s purposes) (case's `charity test facts`)
        address MEANS `Int IP17 the entity has a principal address in Jersey` readings entity (case's `facts for the principal address`)
        undesirable MEANS `Int IP18 the name is undesirable` readings (case's `opinion on the name`)
        complied MEANS `Int IP22 the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` (case's `the application states that the entity holds declarations`) (`Int the people who are governors` readings vintage (case's body))
        bars MEANS `Int IP23 Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (`Int the people who are governors` readings vintage (case's body))
        ordered MEANS `Int IP24 the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` readings (case's `orders of the court`) day
        orderB MEANS `Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies` readings (case's `Order under Article 13(9)`) (case's `relief Orders under Article 13(10)`)
        duty MEANS `Art 11 the duty of the Commissioner on the application` (readings's `reading of Articles 11 and 12`) (case's application) orderB complied entity charityTest (case's findings) address undesirable bars ordered

-- The Articles the question rests on, as now numbered.
`Int (a) the units the question rests on` MEANS
    LIST `Int Article` 2, `Int Article` 5, `Int Article` 6, `Int Article` 7, `Int Article` 8, `Int Article` 11, `Int Article` 12, `Int Article` 19, `Int Article` 20

@export May an application for registration as a charity be granted: the Commissioner must register the applicant (Article 11(4)) when the application is complete (Articles 11(2) and 19(5)), the entity meets the charity test (Article 5), is a Jersey entity or has a substantial activity in Jersey, has a principal address in Jersey (Article 8(4)) and a name that is not undesirable (Article 12(1)), and neither a reported fitness issue about a governor (Article 19(9)(c)) nor a court order (Article 20(1)(c)) bars the grant. Refuses for a day before Parts 4 and 5 of the Law were in force (1 May 2018), and for a day on which the text of the Law changed and the two texts answer differently
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups (the favoured readings are `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`)
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked, for example 2026-10-02 (ISO 8601)
      case IS AN `Application in the case` @desc The applicant, its application, and the facts and opinions the Articles read
GIVETH AN `Answer on an application for registration`
`Int (a) may the application be granted` readings day case MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` `Int (a) the units the question rests on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Int the answer under every text of the Law in force on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
            (GIVEN vintage YIELD `Int (a) the answer on the application under the text` readings day vintage case))
